#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:151
msgid "Each enabled email is sent once per order, a set number of days after the order reaches the chosen status. A daily background task finds due orders and sends them. The order is marked before the email is handed over, so a run that dies halfway through cannot quietly send it again every day."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %1$s: date of the cut-off before which orders are never followed up. %2$s: maximum emails per type per run.
#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:157
#, php-format
msgid "No order placed before %1$s is ever followed up, so the customers who ordered before then were not mailed. That date is as far back as the sender reaches, not a promise about every order after it. Each daily run sends at most %2$s emails per type, oldest orders first."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: maximum emails per type per run.
#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:164
#, php-format
msgid "No order placed before this plugin started running here is ever followed up, so the customers who ordered before then were not mailed. That moment is as far back as the sender reaches, not a promise about every order after it. Each daily run sends at most %s emails per type, oldest orders first."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: date the plugin was last switched back on.
#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:173
#, php-format
msgid "The plugin was last switched back on %s, and from that moment each email reaches back by its own delay and no further, so orders that passed their delay while it was off are left alone as well."
msgstr ""

